  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Lang Ya land spirit names the Immortal Gu Connect Luck when Fang Yuan shows it among gains from Eighty-Eight True Yang Building. He recalls that his main body once saw this Gu while discussing cultivation with Giant Sun Immortal Venerable.",
        "chapters": [
          663
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_lang_ya_land_spirit",
          "sys_immortal_gu",
          "char_fang_yuan",
          "house_eighty_eight_true_yang_building",
          "char_giant_sun_immortal_venerable"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan ranks it above Cleanse Soul among those spoils, because it can offset Spring Autumn Cicada’s lasting drain on the owner’s luck.",
        "chapters": [
          664
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_cleanse_soul",
          "gu_spring_autumn_cicada"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Connect Luck, Break Luck, and Divert Disaster belong to the all living being’s luck true inheritance that sat in Imperial Court blessed land. After that blessed land is destroyed, some of those Immortal Gu leave it, while the cultivation details of the inheritance are already lost.",
        "chapters": [
          1051
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "inheritance-and-holders",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_break_luck",
          "gu_divert_disaster_immortal_gu",
          "loc_imperial_court_blessed_land"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan’s own reflection places Connect Luck, Calamity Beckoning, and Fortune Rivalling Heaven in that same true inheritance.",
        "chapters": [
          1093
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "inheritance-and-holders",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_calamity_beckoning_gu",
          "gu_fortune_rivalling_heaven_immortal_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Separate narration during Feng Jun’s luck whirlwind states Fang Yuan once possessed Connect Luck as part of all living being’s luck, which Giant Sun Immortal Venerable placed in Eighty-Eight True Yang Building.",
        "chapters": [
          1126
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "inheritance-and-holders",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_feng_jun"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Ying Wu Xie has already placed connect luck Immortal Gu in treasure yellow heaven, and with that heaven closed the Gu is trapped there, so it is not among the Immortal Gu Fang Yuan gains in their transaction.",
        "chapters": [
          1079
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "inheritance-and-holders",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_ying_wu_xie"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "When treasure yellow heaven opens again, Ying Wu Xie takes the Gu back; Connect Luck’s effect also targets the soul, so Fang Yuan’s existing luck links remain after he changes body.",
        "chapters": [
          1153
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "inheritance-and-holders",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "A later inventory lists Connect Luck among Fang Yuan’s rank six luck path Immortal Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          1482
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "inheritance-and-holders",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "At the turbulent flow sea, Ying Wu Xie’s luck inspection Immortal Gu shows Fang Yuan’s luck matching his own and Hei Lou Lan’s: Ying Wu Xie had used Connect Luck on Hei Lou Lan, and Hei Lou Lan was already luck connected to Fang Yuan, exposing him despite his changed appearance.",
        "chapters": [
          1151
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "exposure-through-the-luck-link",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_luck_inspection_immortal_gu",
          "char_hei_lou_lan"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Later in Southern Border, narration notes that while Fang Yuan hides inside his placed-down sovereign blessed land, deductions against him become extremely difficult unless someone has clues like those from Connect Luck.",
        "chapters": [
          1321
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "exposure-through-the-luck-link",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "reg_southern_border"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Weighing whether to destroy Shadow Sect, Fang Yuan counts getting rid of Connect Luck’s weakness among his reasons to eliminate them.",
        "chapters": [
          1354
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "exposure-through-the-luck-link",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "fac_shadow_sect"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
